# Build context for the backend image.
#
# This is a SECURITY control, not just a speed tweak. Without it, every byte of
# the working tree is uploaded to the Docker daemon before the build starts -
# which includes Backend/.env (SECRET_KEY, DATABASE_URL, CLOUDINARY_URL),
# .git/ (the full history), Backend/.venv/ and Web_Frontend/node_modules/.
#
# Keep this in sync with .gitignore, but note the two differ on purpose: this
# file describes what the IMAGE needs, .gitignore describes what the repo needs.

# --- Secrets. Must never reach a layer, not even a deleted one. ---
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
Backend/.env*
Backend/.env.example
session-ses_eea3.md
Web_Frontend/node_modules/
TECH.md
dev.ps1
gst_billing_app_specification.md
# --- VCS and CI ---
.git
.gitignore
.github
.claude

# --- Python local env + caches ---
Backend/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.pyo
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/*.egg-info
**/.mypy_cache

# --- Local databases: never bake a developer's data into an image ---
**/*.sqlite3
**/*.sqlite3-journal
**/db.sqlite3

# --- Collectstatic output and uploads are runtime concerns ---
# STATIC_ROOT is produced by `collectstatic` inside the image. Shipping the
# host's copy would bake in absolute paths from a different machine.
Backend/staticfiles
Backend/media

# --- Frontend is served separately (Cloudflare Pages), not by Django ---
Web_Frontend

# --- Docs and scratch: not needed to serve the API ---
Docs
docs
*.md
session-ses_eea3.md
dev.ps1

# --- Editors / OS ---
.vscode
.idea
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
*.log